1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:07,060
[Prof. Peter Kim] On Slide 35, we define our 3-Tier Governance Spectrum for balancing autonomy and control.

2
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:13,680
[TA Sarah Jenkins] This is the golden rule of agent architecture. Not all tasks carry the same risk!

3
00:00:14,080 --> 00:00:28,550
[Prof. Peter Kim] Tier 1 is Full Autonomy. These are low-risk, read-only tasks—like scanning RSS feeds, organizing folder tags, or reading research papers. Let your avatar run freely!

4
00:00:28,950 --> 00:00:41,890
[TA Sarah Jenkins] Tier 2 is Notify & Log. Medium-risk tasks—like drafting customer emails or generating code branches. The avatar performs the work and logs it, notifying you of the outcome.

5
00:00:42,290 --> 00:00:58,800
[Prof. Peter Kim] Tier 3 is Strict Human Approval. High-risk write operations—like sending emails to clients, executing live database migrations, or spending money. The avatar prepares everything, but waits for your explicit click to send!

6
00:00:59,200 --> 00:01:04,790
[TA Sarah Jenkins] This 3-tier matrix eliminates risk while preserving 90% of the speed benefits.

